{
  "about": "Shots (`do`) run with no model against the fixtures in bench/fixture: `watch` (node:test tests that fail on purpose, a stand-in linter, scripts that must not run) and `typecheck` (a TypeScript package with five type errors, one in a folder whose name has a space). The `q` questions are kinds agents answer by hand with npm, pnpm, tsc and test runners: did the tests pass and which failed, is the typecheck clean, what do the package's scripts run and which Node version it expects. They are put to these fixtures; paths in them are relative to the kit's folder. Expectations were checked against the scripts' output on 2026-11-21.",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "commands",
      "do": "commands",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch"
      },
      "expect": [
        "\"name\": \"test\"",
        "npm run test:clacks",
        "\"name\": \"lint\"",
        "it does not end",
        "it changes things"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "run-test",
      "do": "run",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "test"
      },
      "expect": [
        "test failed: 2 of 5 tests",
        "Cable Street has two officers",
        "roster\\.test\\.mjs",
        "\"line\": 10",
        "Nobby is missing from Cable Street"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "run-lint",
      "do": "run",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "lint"
      },
      "expect": [
        "lint failed: 2 errors",
        "roster\\.mjs",
        "throw a WatchError"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "run-build",
      "do": "run",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "build"
      },
      "expect": [
        "build passed",
        "\"ok\": true"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "all",
      "do": "all",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch"
      },
      "expect": [
        "2 of 3 checks failed",
        "lint \\(2 failures\\)",
        "test \\(2 failures\\)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "last",
      "do": "last",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "test"
      },
      "expect": [
        "test failed \\(2\\)",
        "Cable Street has two officers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "failure",
      "do": "failure",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "find": "Nobby is on the roster"
      },
      "expect": [
        "TypeError",
        "Nobby is missing from Cable Street",
        "roster\\.test\\.mjs:22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "flaky",
      "do": "flaky",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "test:clacks",
        "times": 2
      },
      "expect": [
        "flaky: 1 failed in some of 2 runs",
        "the clacks message arrives 1/2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "run-test-expected",
      "do": "run",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch",
        "check": "test"
      },
      "expect": [
        "\"expected\": \"2\"",
        "\"received\": \"1\"",
        "\"operator\": \"strictEqual\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "typecheck",
      "do": "run",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/typecheck",
        "check": "typecheck"
      },
      "expect": [
        "typecheck failed: 5 errors in 3 files",
        "\"code\": \"TS2307\"",
        "src/night watch/beat\\.ts",
        "\"col\": 80",
        "Types of parameters 'post' and 'post' are incompatible",
        "\"src/officer\\.ts\": 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scripts-node",
      "do": "commands",
      "params": {
        "dir": "bench/fixture/watch"
      },
      "expect": [
        "\"manager\": \"npm\"",
        "node --test roster\\.test\\.mjs",
        ">=22\\.13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "failing-tests-q",
      "q": "Do the tests in bench/fixture/watch pass? For each failure give the test, file:line and what was expected against what was received.",
      "expect": [
        "Cable Street has two officers",
        "roster\\.test\\.mjs[\\s\\S]{0,20}\\b10\\b",
        "Nobby is missing from Cable Street",
        "roster\\.test\\.mjs[\\s\\S]{0,20}\\b22\\b"
      ],
      "any": [
        "expected[^.\\n]{0,30}\\b2\\b",
        "\\b2\\b[^.\\n]{0,30}expected"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "type-errors-q",
      "q": "Does the package in bench/fixture/typecheck type-check? List each error with file:line and TS code.",
      "expect": [
        "officer\\.ts[\\s\\S]{0,150}\\b2\\b",
        "TS2322",
        "TS2307",
        "night watch/beat\\.ts",
        "duty\\.ts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scripts-q",
      "q": "In bench/fixture/watch, what does `npm test` run, and which Node version does the package expect?",
      "expect": [
        "roster\\.test\\.mjs",
        "22\\.13"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
